WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:03.030
Film Courage: Robin, what were some mistakes
you made early on coming here [to Los Angeles]

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:10.890
and in your career that maybe weren’t horrible
mistakes but had you known, you wouldn’t

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:11.890
have done.

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:17.539
Whether it was spending too much time thinking
about this or that or whatever?

00:00:17.539 --> 00:00:19.869
Robin Riker: Yeah…okay.

00:00:19.869 --> 00:00:28.449
There was…at one of my early jobs was on
[the TV show] Fantasy Island.

00:00:28.449 --> 00:00:40.190
I was among a retinue of young women who were
surrounding this older man, the guest star

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:41.500
of the show.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:49.649
And so we broke for lunch and I had lines
(this other woman didn’t have lines).

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:53.670
But we were walking to lunch and she was a
goddess!

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:57.980
She was so beautiful and very sweet and really
lovely.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:01.550
And we were just talking and I liked her right
away and she started to tell me about her

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:02.550
husband.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:09.620
And immediately I got this overwhelming sense
of dread on her behalf…I mean I have chills

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.470
now even remembering it.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:16.700
And she had been working at a Dairy Queen
in Canada or something.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:22.210
And he was older than she and he spotted her
and he saw what she was and got her into Playboy

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:28.010
and she had a Playboy centerfold spot.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:33.380
And the more she talked about him, the creepier
I felt about this guy.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.250
But I mean, we just met each other, what am
I going to say about her husband?

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:39.530
I mean “You better watch out for him.”

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:42.500
And then I learned that she was with my agency.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:47.840
Then about a week or month later maybe, I’m
walking with my agent to an audition and he

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.300
tells me that this woman just got a part in
a major motion picture.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:57.530
Now I have been a classically trained actress
since I was two years old and she had just

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:58.700
blown into town.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:01:59.970
Now she was a goddess.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:03.420
I have to give you that and Hollywood eats
that up.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.450
But I was so jealous!

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.150
I couldn’t believe it.

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:13.460
I was just churning with envy inside and resentment!

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:17.040
And it felt like…oh it was awful!

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.460
About two months after that I was going to
New York, I had a play that I was taking to

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.590
New York that I wanted to shop it around a
bit.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:30.700
And I’m walking home and I see a headline
you know ‘Beauty Queen Slain!’

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:33.730
And I thought ‘Oh it was some Miss New Jersey
or something.’

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:34.730
I didn’t pay any attention.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:37.100
I called my agents to find out what was going
on, if I should come in for something.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.730
And they said “Oh, we’re just so upset
about Dorothy.”

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:44.520
And I put on my best…I tried my best to
care.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.400
And I said “Oh really, why?”

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.680
And they said “Didn’t you hear?

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:53.560
Her husband just shot her in the face and
murdered her because she was drifting away

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:54.560
from him.”

00:02:54.560 --> 00:03:00.440
It was Dorothy Stratten who was the subject
of the film STAR 80.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:16.400
And even now…you see…I was so ashamed
of myself for begrudging her one moment of

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:26.680
celebrity or joy because I had no idea what
lay before her and I had no idea what she

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:32.400
went through to get that, to get there…to
her moment in the sun.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:36.319
And how dare I?

00:03:36.319 --> 00:03:46.850
How dare I and that was…I was more affected
by her death and what it called up in me then

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:52.950
I was when my own grandfather died because
I was so ashamed of my jealousy.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:58.140
Film Courage: Did you know I was actually
going to bring that story up…I mean I have

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.140
chills right now.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:02.770
I did not know you were going to go there.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:05.290
I was going to bring up the Dorothy Stratten
movie…

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:06.650
Robin Riker: Oh, my God.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:07.650
Really?

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.370
Film Courage: This is so….I have chills
right now and I was going to talk about that.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:11.590
And I didn’t even know…

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:12.590
Robin Riker: Wow!

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:15.140
So when I said the word “Dorothy” you
went like [imitates deep breath] like that.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.320
Film Courage: Yeah…it just hit me.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.320
I have chills right now.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:22.800
Robin Riker: Well that was one of the biggest
mistakes I ever made and boy did it change

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:23.800
me.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:30.550
Film Courage: I remember seeing the movie
and…yeah…it’s very sad.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:33.559
Robin Riker: And she was such a lovely girl.

00:04:33.559 --> 00:04:37.539
She was such a genuinely sweet person, you
know?

00:04:37.539 --> 00:04:39.490
Film Courage: Yeah…I didn’t know her but…

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:41.050
Robin Riker: She wasn’t a climber.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:46.270
She took advantage of the opportunities that
came to her and so she should of and so would

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.270
we all!

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:48.270
Film Courage: Right.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.270
We all would, that’s the thing.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:55.659
Robin Riker: And oh, that little bitter part
of me…I just couldn’t…

00:04:55.659 --> 00:05:02.270
Film Courage: Well I think as younger women
we’re trained to be competitive in some

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:03.940
sense or maybe this town [Los Angeles]…I
know we talked about this before.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:04.940
Robin Riker: The culture of this town.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:05.940
Film Courage: Right.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:06.940
The culture of this town.

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:11.159
So I think (unfortunately) it’s somewhat
normal.

00:05:11.159 --> 00:05:15.089
Being in grade school or whenever you can
just remember feeling the same way toward

00:05:15.089 --> 00:05:17.892
someone and I think being honest enough to
talk about it is important.

00:05:17.892 --> 00:05:22.479
I know Marc Maron is always bashed about his
talk for being jealous toward something.

00:05:22.479 --> 00:05:26.409
I actually think it’s healthy that he’s
able to admit that, when I think a lot of

00:05:26.409 --> 00:05:27.930
people feel it.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:34.589
So you just happened to have an experience
that is so powerful.

00:05:34.589 --> 00:05:36.919
Most situations don’t end up that way.

00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:37.919
Wow!

00:05:37.919 --> 00:05:40.150
I was literally going to bring that up.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:41.360
Robin Riker: Mind melt!

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:46.449
Film Courage: And for anyone who doesn’t
know the Dorothy Stratten story, I encourage

00:05:46.449 --> 00:05:48.539
them to look it up just as a way to…

00:05:48.539 --> 00:05:53.129
Robin Riker: As a little primer for what can
happen.

00:05:53.129 --> 00:06:00.360
Film Courage: And comparing outsides…or
other people’s outsides to our insides,

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.659
especially in this town and we never know.

00:06:02.659 --> 00:06:07.190
Robin Riker: And when I said a primer of what
can happen, I don’t mean the result of what

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:08.259
happened to her.

00:06:08.259 --> 00:06:18.330
But I just mean what can happen to you when
you resent and bear jealousy and envy toward

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:24.039
someone who has nothing at all to do with
you or your life or your trajectory in this

00:06:24.039 --> 00:06:25.039
life.

00:06:25.039 --> 00:06:30.240
Film Courage: I think as time goes on and
we go out for things (whatever our chosen

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:34.740
pursuit is) and we don’t get them and we
see other people get them, it’s just natural

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:37.779
that it’s going to happen and we’re going
to feel upset.

00:06:37.779 --> 00:06:41.330
And I think to cycle through it and to be
“Okay, I feel it and now I’m going to

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:42.330
let it go now.”

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:43.330
Robin Riker: Exactly, feel it.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:45.080
It’s inhuman not to feel it.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:46.580
We have to feel it.

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.900
But we don’t have to live in it.

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:52.610
I mean feel it, live in it and be disappointed
(it’s disappointing).

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:56.620
But you live to bat another day, you know?

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.330
Film Courage: Wow.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:06:59.330
Yeah.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:00.330
That’s quite a story.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:01.809
Quite a story.

00:07:01.809 --> 00:07:02.909
Thank you.

